---
![ходьба на улице](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0d2cdcb2-ddfc-429f-8915-33670f9ce7b2)

{{% steps %}}

### Step 1
Stand tall with your chest up and shoulders back—avoid slouching. Gently engage your core and lower back muscles, as if taking a deep breath.

### Step 2
Bend your elbows at a 90-degree angle, loosely curl your hands into relaxed fists, and swing your arms naturally in rhythm with each step.

### Step 3
With each stride, straighten your front leg as it moves forward, while letting your trailing leg bend naturally at the knee.

### Step 4
Keep your chin lifted and look about 10–15 meters (30–50 feet) ahead of you.

### Step 5
When you take a step, land gently on your heel first, roll smoothly through the middle of the foot, and push off with your toes. At the same time, use your back foot to push off from the ball of the foot and toes. This heel-to-toe roll is the most important part of proper walking technique.

### Step 6
Transfer your body weight evenly from the heel through to the big toe with every step. Keep your feet pointing straight ahead—do not point your toes outward.

{{% /steps %}}

{{< callout type="info" >}}
• Wear comfortable clothing and supportive athletic shoes.

• Walk in areas with clean, fresh air; try to avoid noisy, busy roads.

• Always start at an easy, slow pace, gradually increase your walking speed, and slow down again near the end to cool down.
{{< /callout >}}
